[al:新概念英语第二册]
[ti:A Cold Welcome]
[00:00.68]What does 'a cold welcome' refer to? | “冷淡的欢迎”指的是什么？
[00:14.18]On Wednesday evening, we went to the Town Hall. | 星期三晚上，我们去了市政厅。
[00:19.08]It was the last day of the year | 那是今年的最后一天，
[00:21.69]and a large crowd of people had gathered under the Town Hall clock. | 一大群人聚集在市政厅大钟下面。
[00:26.92]It would strike twelve in twenty minutes' time. | 再过二十分钟，大钟就要敲响十二点了。
[00:30.98]Fifteen minutes passed and then, | 十五分钟过去了，接着，
[00:33.97]at five to twelve, the clock stopped. | 在十二点差五分的时候，大钟停了。
[00:37.54]The big minute hand did not move. | 巨大的分针一动不动。
[00:40.54]We waited and waited, | 我们等啊等，
[00:43.02]but nothing happened. | 但什么也没有发生。
[00:44.74]Suddenly someone shouted. | 突然有人喊道：
[00:47.36]'It's two minutes past twelve! | “已经十二点过两分了！
[00:50.43]The clock has stopped!' | 大钟停了！”
[00:52.60]I looked at my watch. | 我看了看我的表。
[00:54.60]It was true. | 果然如此。
[00:56.06]The big clock refused to welcome the New Year. | 那座大钟拒不迎接新年。
[01:00.32]At that moment, everybody began to laugh and sing. | 就在那一刻，所有人都开始笑啊唱啊。